1
00:00:00,180 --> 00:00:01,104
Trade goods.

2
00:00:01,104 --> 00:00:02,489
Choose your route.

3
00:00:02,489 --> 00:00:03,644
Risk an ambush.

4
00:00:03,644 --> 00:00:08,416
This is Frontier, a strategy and trading game on NEAR testnet.

5
00:00:08,416 --> 00:00:12,110
These are real transactions in the deployed app.

6
00:00:12,460 --> 00:00:17,091
For this recording, an automated testnet wallet approves a game-only key.

7
00:00:17,091 --> 00:00:19,565
The key is restricted to this contract.

8
00:00:19,565 --> 00:00:25,020
Registering gives our new captain one thousand CRED, the non-redeemable game currency.

9
00:00:25,370 --> 00:00:29,652
The port market reads its reserves and owner fee from the contract.

10
00:00:29,652 --> 00:00:33,551
We spend three hundred CRED on Hashpower, then build a sloop.

11
00:00:33,551 --> 00:00:37,450
Every purchase changes the market and our on-chain inventory.

12
00:00:37,800 --> 00:00:43,336
We load 41 units of Hashpower and seal the destination with a browser-generated salt.

13
00:00:43,336 --> 00:00:46,983
A scripted rival has placed a real ambush on this route.

14
00:00:46,983 --> 00:00:50,890
The backup download preserves the secret needed for arrival.

15
00:00:51,240 --> 00:00:55,000
Once the travel time passes, we reveal the destination.

16
00:00:55,000 --> 00:00:58,896
The contract validates the route and resolves the ambush.

17
00:00:58,896 --> 00:01:02,177
The result feed reports the raid and cargo loss.

18
00:01:02,177 --> 00:01:04,980
These outcomes come from contract events.

19
00:01:05,330 --> 00:01:10,380
Back at the market panel, we sell the surviving Hashpower at the current quote.

20
00:01:10,380 --> 00:01:12,362
The CRED balance changes again.

21
00:01:12,362 --> 00:01:17,540
This run shows the cost of fees and a raid; it does not promise a trading profit.

22
00:01:17,890 --> 00:01:20,129
A player can also become a raider.

23
00:01:20,129 --> 00:01:25,265
We choose another route, stake ten CRED, save the salt, and reveal the ambush.

24
00:01:25,265 --> 00:01:29,940
The browser exposes the reveal control and keeps a downloadable backup.

25
00:01:30,290 --> 00:01:34,670
The economy panel reads live supply, faucet, and spoilage totals.

26
00:01:34,670 --> 00:01:37,635
Ports collect trading fees for their owners.

27
00:01:37,635 --> 00:01:44,440
This is a testnet MVP; cross-chain Intents settlement and production season rollover are future work.

28
00:01:44,790 --> 00:01:47,380
Try Frontier at the link on screen.

29
00:01:47,380 --> 00:01:52,561
The repository includes the contract, tests, and transaction evidence.

30
00:01:52,561 --> 00:01:54,338
Built at NEAR Hackathon.

31
00:01:54,338 --> 00:01:57,520
Synthetic narration; real testnet gameplay.
